KeepsGroupTimeout() {","+\t\tThreadPoolTaskScheduler taskScheduler = new ThreadPoolTaskScheduler();","+\t\ttaskScheduler.afterPropertiesSet();","+\t\ttry {","+\t\t\tQueueChannel replyChannel = new QueueChannel();","+\t\t\tQueueChannel discardChannel = new QueueChannel();","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setReleasePartialSequences(true);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setSendPartialResultOnExpiry(true);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setOutputChannel(replyChannel);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setDiscardChannel(discardChannel);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setTaskScheduler(taskScheduler);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setGroupTimeoutExpression(new SpelExpressionParser().parseExpression(\"500\"));","+","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"alpha\", \"ABC\", 4, 1, null));","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"charlie\", \"ABC\", 4, 3, null));","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"alpha-redelivered\", \"ABC\", 4, 1, null));","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"charlie-redelivered\", \"ABC\", 4, 3, null));","+","+\t\t\tassertThat(replyChannel.receive(0)).extracting(\"payload\").isEqualTo(\"alpha\");","+\t\t\tassertThat(replyChannel.receive(10_000)).extracting(\"payload\").isEqualTo(\"charlie\");","+\t\t\tassertThat(discardChannel.clear()).extracting(\"payload\")","+\t\t\t\t\t.containsExactly(\"alpha-redelivered\", \"charlie-redelivered\");","+\t\t}","+\t\tfinally {","+\t\t\ttaskScheduler.destroy();","+\t\t}","+\t}","+","+\t@Test","+\tpublic void testPartialReleaseWithGroupCondition() {","+\t\tQueueChannel replyChannel = new QueueChannel();","+\t\tthis.resequencer.setReleasePartialSequences(true);","+\t\tthis.resequencer.setOutputChannel(replyChannel);","+\t\tthis.resequencer.setGroupConditionSupplier((message, existing) -> \"open\");","+","+\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"alpha\", \"ABC\", 4, 1, null));","+\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"bravo\", \"ABC\", 4, 2, null));","+\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"charlie\", \"ABC\", 4, 3, null));","+","+\t\tassertThat(replyChannel.clear()).extracting(\"payload\").containsExactly(\"alpha\", \"bravo\", \"charlie\");","+\t}","+","+\t@Test","+\tpublic void testPartialReleaseWithGroupConditionKeepsGroupTimeout() {","+\t\tThreadPoolTaskScheduler taskScheduler = new ThreadPoolTaskScheduler();","+\t\ttaskScheduler.afterPropertiesSet();","+\t\ttry {","+\t\t\tQueueChannel replyChannel = new QueueChannel();","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setReleasePartialSequences(true);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setSendPartialResultOnExpiry(true);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setOutputChannel(replyChannel);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setTaskScheduler(taskScheduler);","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setGroupTimeoutExpression(","+\t\t\t\t\tnew SpelExpressionParser().parseExpression(\"condition == 'open' ? 500 : null\"));","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.setGroupConditionSupplier((message, existing) -> \"open\");","+","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"alpha\", \"ABC\", 4, 1, null));","+\t\t\tthis.resequencer.handleMessage(createMessage(\"charlie\", \"ABC\", 4, 3, null));","+","+\t\t\tassertThat(replyChannel.receive(0)).extracting(\"payload\").isEqualTo(\"alpha\");","+\t\t\tassertThat(replyChannel.receive(10_000)).extracting(\"payload\").isEqualTo(\"charlie\");","+\t\t}","+\t\tfinally {","+\t\t\ttaskScheduler.destroy();","+\t\t}","+\t}","+"," \tprivate static Message<?> createMessage(String payload, Object correlationId, int sequenceSize, int sequenceNumber,"," \t\t\tMessageChannel replyChannel) {"," "],"additions":89,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/reference/antora/modules/ROOT/pages/aggregator.adoc","lines":["@@ -473,9 +473,10 @@ By default, an internal `DefaultLockRegistry` is used."," Use of a distributed `LockRegistry`, such as the `ZookeeperLockRegistry`, ensures only one instance of the aggregator can operate on a group concurrently."," See xref:redis.adoc#redis-lock-registry[Redis Lock Registry] or xref:zookeeper.adoc#zk-lock-registry[Zookeeper Lock Registry] for more information."," <21> A timeout (in milliseconds) to force the `MessageGroup` complete when the `ReleaseStrategy` does not release the group when the current message arrives.","-This attribute provides a built-in time-based release strategy for the aggregator when there is a need to emit a partial result (or discard the group) if a new message does not arrive for the `MessageGroup` within the timeout which counts from the time the last message arrived.","+This attribute provides a built-in time-based release strategy for the aggregator when there is a need to emit a partial result (or discard the group) if no new message is added to the `MessageGroup` within the timeout, counted from the time the last message was added."," To set up a timeout which counts from the time the `MessageGroup` was created see `group-timeout-expression` information.","-When a new message arrives at the aggregator, any existing `ScheduledFuture<?>` for its `MessageGroup` is canceled.","+When a new message is added to its `MessageGroup`, any existing `ScheduledFuture<?>` for that group is canceled.","+A discarded message (for example, a late-arriving one) does not cancel it."," If the `ReleaseStrategy` returns `false` (meaning do not release) and `groupTimeout > 0`, a new task is scheduled to expire the group."," We do not advise setting this attribute to zero (or a negative value)."," Doing so effectively disables the aggregator because every message group is immediately completed.","@@ -498,7 +499,7 @@ Late arriving messages start a new group."," You can set this to `false` to complete the group but have its metadata remain so that late arriving messages are discarded."," Empty groups can be expired later using a `MessageGroupStoreReaper` together with the `empty-group-min-timeout` attribute."," It defaults to 'true'.","-<24> A `TaskScheduler` bean reference to schedule the `MessageGroup` to be forced complete if no new message arrives for the `MessageGroup` within the `groupTimeout`.","+<24> A `TaskScheduler` bean reference to schedule the `MessageGroup` to be forced complete if no new message is added to the `MessageGroup` within the `groupTimeout`."," If not provided, the default scheduler (`taskScheduler`) registered in the `ApplicationContext` (`ThreadPoolTaskScheduler`) is used."," This attribute does not apply if `group-timeout` or `group-timeout-expression` is not specified."," <25> Since version 4.1."],"additions":4,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/reference/antora/modules/ROOT/pages/resequencer.adoc","lines":["@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ The following example shows a resequencer configuration:"," Required."," <3> The channel to which the resequencer sends the reordered messages."," Optional.","-<4> The channel to which the resequencer  sends the messages that timed out (if `send-partial-result-on-timeout` is set to `false`).","+<4> The channel to which the resequencer sends the messages that timed out (if `send-partial-result-on-expiry` is set to `false`), and late or duplicate messages, including those whose sequence number is at or below the last released one when `release-partial-sequences` is `true`."," Optional."," <5> Whether to send out ordered sequences as soon as they are available or only after the whole message group arrives."," Optional.",""],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false}],"additions":134,"deletions":9,"truncated":false,"file_count":6},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-24T20:29:56.479486+00:00"}